connected to target database: XE (DBID=3062123222)

RMAN> # =====================================================================
2> # PROJECT 3 - PART 2 of 3: RMAN configuration and the full backup
3> #
4> # Run with:   rman target /
5> # =====================================================================
6> 
7> # ---------------------------------------------------------------------
8> # 1. RMAN persistent configuration
9> # ---------------------------------------------------------------------
10> 
11> # Keep two full copies of every datafile before anything becomes obsolete
12> CONFIGURE RETENTION POLICY TO REDUNDANCY 2;
13> 
14> # Control file autobackup - REQUIRED by the project brief.
15> # It makes RMAN write a copy of the control file and the spfile after
16> # every backup and after any structural change. Without it, losing the
17> # control file means recovery has to start from a manual copy.
18> CONFIGURE CONTROLFILE AUTOBACKUP ON;
19> CONFIGURE CONTROLFILE AUTOBACKUP FORMAT FOR DEVICE TYPE DISK TO '/u01/app/oracle/fast_recovery_area/autobackup_%F';
20> 
21> # Disk as the default device, with a readable naming pattern
22> CONFIGURE DEFAULT DEVICE TYPE TO DISK;
23> CONFIGURE DEVICE TYPE DISK PARALLELISM 1 BACKUP TYPE TO BACKUPSET;
24> CONFIGURE CHANNEL DEVICE TYPE DISK FORMAT '/u01/app/oracle/fast_recovery_area/%U';
25> 
26> # Do not back up a block more than once if it has not changed
27> CONFIGURE BACKUP OPTIMIZATION ON;
28> 
29> # Show the resulting configuration - good screenshot for the report
30> SHOW ALL;
31> 
32> # ---------------------------------------------------------------------
33> # 2. FULL BACKUP of the whole database, plus the archived redo logs.
34> #    "PLUS ARCHIVELOG" matters: without the archived logs the datafile
35> #    backup cannot be rolled forward to a consistent point in time.
36> # ---------------------------------------------------------------------
37> BACKUP DATABASE PLUS ARCHIVELOG;
38> 
39> # ---------------------------------------------------------------------
40> # 3. Prove the backup exists
41> # ---------------------------------------------------------------------
42> LIST BACKUP SUMMARY;
43> 
44> REPORT SCHEMA;
45> 
46> EXIT;
